<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The debug build keeps its files apart from the release build's, as it
        keeps its package, its settings and its storage permission apart.

        It has to. The two are different packages and so different uids, and
        scoped storage hands an app only the files it wrote itself: pointed at
        one folder, whichever installed second sees an empty one it cannot even
        write into, because the names it wants are taken by files it is not
        allowed to see. That reads as "ROMs needed" on a machine where the
        release build ran first, and nothing says why.

        No space in the name, deliberately: every adb command, script and doc
        that names the folder would need quoting, and one that forgot would list
        the release build's folder instead and look like it had worked.
    -->
    <string name="data_folder" translatable="false">Zedex-debug</string>
</resources>
